    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. (1) It does not say `real: axiom=30` moved; it did not. The ledger still pins the axiom declarations, and moving the pin onto the telescope is a separate change (ADR-0515, 'What this ADR does not do'). (2) It does not say \u2124 is \u211d. The interface has no inverse, no completeness and no Archimedean axiom, so both developments satisfy it; ADR-0456's caveat stands. (3) It compares RENDERED types, which is what the ledger digests \u2014 not definitional equality, and not the proofs. That the `Int` side's 30 are proved rather than assumed is the separate measurement `integer: axiom=0` in nat_axiom_inventory. (4) The comparison is positional: it pairs binder i with binder i, so it would not notice two interface slots being swapped in BOTH signatures at once. It does notice a swap in one of them \u2014 measured, transposing `le_refl`/`le_trans` in `From<IntPrelude>` gives '28 identical, 2 differing' and exit 1, which is the transposition an earlier lane found no test could see.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
